# Ruby 3.4.7 for Cosmopolitan Libc (CosmoRuby)

**Status**: Beta Release (Functional, not production-ready)
**Version**: Ruby 3.4.7 on Cosmopolitan Libc
**Last Updated**: 2025-10-23

## What is CosmoRuby?

CosmoRuby is Ruby 3.4.7 ported to Cosmopolitan Libc, creating Actually Portable Executables that run natively on:
- Linux (x86_64, aarch64)
- macOS (x86_64, arm64)
- Windows (x86_64)
- FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD

**One binary. Runs everywhere. No installation. No dependencies.**

## Quick Start

### Download the Binaries

Get `ruby.com`, `irb.com`, and `gem.com` from the release.

### Run Ruby

```bash
# Make executable
chmod +x ruby.com

# Run a script
./ruby.com script.rb

# Run a one-liner
./ruby.com -e "puts 'Hello, World!'"

# Check version
./ruby.com --version
```

### Run IRB (Interactive Ruby)

```bash
chmod +x irb.com
./irb.com
```

```ruby
>> [1, 2, 3].map { |x| x * 2 }
=> [2, 4, 6]
>> puts "CosmoRuby works!"
CosmoRuby works!
=> nil
```

### Use RubyGems

```bash
chmod +x gem.com

# List installed gems
./gem.com list

# Show gem environment
./gem.com env
```

### Optional: Add to PATH

```bash
# Create ~/bin if it doesn't exist
mkdir -p ~/bin

# Copy or symlink binaries
cp ruby.com irb.com gem.com ~/bin/
# OR
ln -s /full/path/to/ruby.com ~/bin/ruby.com
ln -s /full/path/to/irb.com ~/bin/irb.com
ln -s /full/path/to/gem.com ~/bin/gem.com

# Add to PATH (if not already)
export PATH="$HOME/bin:$PATH"

# Now use without ./
ruby.com --version
irb.com
gem.com list
```

## What Works ✅

### Core Language Features
- ✅ Full Ruby 3.4.7 language (classes, modules, blocks, procs, lambdas)
- ✅ Fibers, threads, ractors (concurrent programming)
- ✅ Garbage collection, marshaling
- ✅ Exception handling with full backtraces
- ✅ All 2005 bootstrap tests passing (100% pass rate)

### Standard Library
- ✅ IRB (interactive shell) with syntax highlighting
- ✅ RubyGems package manager
- ✅ Bundler (v2.6.9) for dependency management
- ✅ 24 pure Ruby gems included:
  - **Build tools**: rake, bundler
  - **Testing**: minitest, test-unit, power_assert
  - **Networking**: net-ftp, net-imap, net-pop, net-smtp
  - **Data**: csv, rexml, rss
  - **Utilities**: abbrev, base64, drb, getoptlong, matrix, mutex_m, observer, prime, repl_type_completor, resolv-replace, rinda, typeprof

### Networking
- ✅ Socket extension (TCP, UDP, Unix sockets)
- ✅ HTTP/HTTPS via net-http (requires openssl gem for HTTPS)
- ✅ Network operations for gem installation

### Extensions (Statically Linked)
- ✅ Ripper (parser introspection)
- ✅ io/console (terminal control)
- ✅ io/wait (non-blocking I/O)
- ✅ monitor (thread synchronization)
- ✅ pathname (path manipulation)
- ✅ stringio (string I/O)
- ✅ socket (networking)

## What Doesn't Work (Yet) ⚠️

### Native Extensions
- ❌ Cannot load gems with C extensions (nokogiri, pg, mysql2, sqlite3, puma, etc.)
- ❌ 6 bundled gems with native extensions don't work:
  - bigdecimal, debug, nkf, racc, rbs, syslog
- ❌ `gem install` for gems requiring compilation will fail

**Why**: Cosmopolitan uses static linking. Dynamic .so loading is planned for future releases.

**Workaround**: Use pure Ruby alternatives when available.

### Performance
- ⚠️ No JIT compiler (YJIT/RJIT disabled)
- ⚠️ Performance ~2-3x slower than YJIT-enabled Ruby
- ⚠️ Acceptable for scripts, tools, development; not optimized for production

### Platform-Specific Features
- ❌ Windows: Some POSIX features may not work perfectly
- ❌ Fork support varies by platform
- ❌ No setlocale() (Cosmopolitan doesn't implement it)

## Common Use Cases

### Scripting
```ruby
#!/usr/bin/env ruby.com

# Your Ruby script here
puts "Portable Ruby script!"
```

### Simple Web Server (Sinatra)
```ruby
# Gemfile
source 'https://rubygems.org'
gem 'sinatra'

# app.rb
require 'sinatra'

get '/' do
  'Hello from CosmoRuby!'
end
```

```bash
# Install (pure Ruby gems only)
gem.com install sinatra rack
ruby.com app.rb
```

### Build Automation (Rake)
```ruby
# Rakefile
task :default => [:test]

task :test do
  puts "Running tests..."
  sh "ruby.com test/test_*.rb"
end

task :deploy do
  puts "Deploying..."
end
```

```bash
ruby.com -S rake test
```

### Command-Line Tools
CosmoRuby is perfect for portable CLI tools that need to run anywhere.

## Troubleshooting

### "ruby.com: command not found"
- Make sure the file is executable: `chmod +x ruby.com`
- Run with `./ruby.com` or add to PATH

### "LoadError: cannot load such file"
- For stdlib: The file should be embedded in ruby.com
- For gems: Install with `gem.com install GEMNAME` (pure Ruby gems only)

### "Permission denied"
```bash
chmod +x ruby.com irb.com gem.com
```

### Gem install fails with "Building native extensions"
Native extension gems are not supported yet. Look for pure Ruby alternatives.

### Slow performance
This is expected without JIT. CosmoRuby prioritizes portability over speed.

## Building from Source

See `docs/ai/RUBY_PORT_PROGRESS.md` for complete build instructions.

**Quick build:**
```bash
# Clone Cosmopolitan repository
git clone https://github.com/jart/cosmopolitan.git
cd cosmopolitan

# Build Ruby
make -j8 o//third_party/ruby/ruby
make -j8 o//third_party/ruby/irb

# Package with embedded stdlib
cd third_party/ruby/port_scripts
bash package_ruby.sh

# Binaries are at:
# o/third_party/ruby/ruby.com
# o/third_party/ruby/irb.com
```

## Known Issues

1. **Native extensions**: Cannot load .so files (planned feature)
2. **Performance**: No JIT compilation available
3. **Some bundled gems**: 6 gems with C extensions don't load
4. **gem install**: Only works for pure Ruby gems
5. **Platform quirks**: Some POSIX features may behave differently on Windows

